STUDENTHUB PORTAL – REQUIREMENT DOCUMENT

Project Overview
StudentHub Portal is a web-based student portal designed to provide students with important academic information in one place. The portal will include courses, attendance, assignments, results, profile details, and contact/support features. The project will first be developed using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript and can be extended with a backend and database later.

Problem Statement
Students often need to check academic information from different places. This can be time-consuming and confusing. StudentHub provides a simple and organized website where students can access their common academic information through a single portal.

Objectives
• Create a simple and user-friendly student portal.
• Provide easy access to academic information.
• Organize courses, attendance, assignments, and results.
• Provide a student dashboard and profile page.
• Create a proper project structure using Git and GitHub.
• Keep the project ready for future backend development.

User Roles
• Student: Can login, view dashboard, courses, attendance, assignments, results, and profile.
• Faculty: Future role for managing courses, attendance, assignments, and results.
• Administrator: Future role for managing students, courses, and portal data.

Functional Requirements
Home page shall display the portal introduction, features, and navigation.
Register page shall allow a new student to enter basic details.
Login page shall provide a student login form.
Dashboard shall show important academic information and quick links.
Courses page shall display enrolled courses and basic course details.
Attendance page shall show overall and subject-wise attendance.
Assignments page shall show assignments, due dates, and status.
Results page shall show semester and subject-wise results.
Profile page shall show basic student and academic information.
Contact page shall provide a form for student queries.
All major pages shall have proper navigation links.
Forms shall have basic input validation using JavaScript.


Required Web Pages
1. Home
2. Login
3. Register
4. Dashboard
5. Courses
6. Attendance
7. Assignments
8. Results
9. Profile
10. Contact

Non-Functional Requirements
• The website should be simple and easy to use.
• The website should be responsive on desktop and mobile screens.
• Pages should load properly and have consistent design.
• Files should be organized into HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and assets folders.
• GitHub should be used to maintain project versions and commits.

Navigation Flow
Home → Login/Register → Dashboard → Courses / Attendance / Assignments / Results / Profile
Home → Contact
Logout → Home/Login

For the initial project, navigation between HTML pages will be handled using links and relative file paths.

Proposed Folder Structure
StudentHubPortal/
├── index.html
├── pages/
├── css/
├── js/
├── assets/
├── docs/
└── README.md

Tools and Technologies
HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript, VS Code, Draw.io/Figma, Git, and GitHub.


